==Aftermath==
Following the results of the second round, Prime Minister and GERB leader [[Boiko Borisov]] tendered his resignation.<ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20161114234645/http://in.reuters.com/article/bulgaria-election-government-idINL8N1DF29T Bulgarian PM Borisov tenders his government resignation] Reuters, 14 November 2016</ref> Two days later, on 16 November, the National Assembly voted 218–0 to accept it, resulting in [[2017 Bulgarian parliamentary election|early parliamentary elections]].<ref>{{cite web|title=Bulgarian MPs Accept PM Borisov's Resignation|url=http://www.novinite.com/articles/177462/Bulgarian+MPs+Accept+PM+Borisov%27s+%3Cb%3EResignation%3C/b%3E|website=Novinite|access-date=17 November 2016|date=16 November 2016|archive-date=15 June 2022|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220615104746/https://www.novinite.com/articles/177462/Bulgarian+MPs+Accept+PM+Borisov%27s+%3Cb%3EResignation%3C/b%3E|url-status=dead}}</ref>

